# Aqil engineering rules

**Non-negotiable:** follow all twelve rules in `docs/AGENT_OPERATING_RULES.md` (read before substantive work; scope; verification; security; approval gates; research integrity; costs; backlog/handover; Git authorisation; build the product — not bureaucracy).

## Documentation authority

- Start with `docs/00_READ_ME_FIRST.md`, `docs/AGENT_OPERATING_RULES.md`, and `docs/DOCUMENTATION_AUTHORITY.md`.
- Canonical specs win over reference material. **`docs/sausage-transfer/` is historical investigation only — never implement from it without a canonical mapping.**
- Workflow: `docs/CURSOR_COLLABORATION_WORKFLOW.md`.
- After substantive work: update `docs/07_BUILD_BACKLOG.csv` and fill `docs/CURSOR_SESSION_HANDOVER.md` (no unsupported “verified” claims).

## Product truth

- JSON Schemas in `docs/schemas/` (mirrored under `packages/contracts/schemas/`) define cross-language contracts.
- Do not invent detailed product requirements, financial narratives, market data or research conclusions in code or UI.

## Change discipline

- Prefer small, scoped diffs. Do not refactor unrelated code.
- Do not add dependencies unless they clearly reduce risk or duplication.
- Classify risk (R0–R3 per `docs/06_ENGINEERING_DISCIPLINE.md`) and run applicable CI gates before claiming work is complete.
- Ask before destructive operations, permission changes, production migrations or security-sensitive changes.

## Repository layout

- Follow `docs/06_ENGINEERING_DISCIPLINE.md` for module boundaries (`apps/web`, `workers/research`, `packages/contracts`, `supabase/migrations`, `supabase/tests/database`).

## Authentication (when implemented)

- Follow `docs/AUTH_AND_SESSION_DOCTRINE.md`: one server-side auth decision per request, `@supabase/ssr` cookies, coalesced refresh, PWA resume, fail-closed private data. Middleware may continue to the server guard on a transport failure; it must not grant access.

## Design system

- `docs/design/tokens.css` is the design authority; `apps/web/src/styles/tokens.css` must stay aligned.
- Responsive shell: `docs/RESPONSIVE_LAYOUT_CONTRACT.md`; layout utilities in `apps/web/src/styles/layout.css`.
- Components use semantic tokens only — no raw hex/RGB/HSL in `apps/web/src` outside `styles/*.css` token files.
- Run `npm run check:tokens` and `npm run test:e2e` after layout changes.

## Data and research integrity

- Facts, inferences, scenarios and predictions must remain distinct (see `docs/00_READ_ME_FIRST.md`).
- Immutable history, versioned models, idempotent ingestion, provenance clocks — `docs/04_ARCHITECTURE_AND_DATA.md`.
- Do not silently change published research history; append corrections and versions.
- `workers/research` claim verification must fail closed until registry checks exist.

## Security and safety

- Follow `docs/INFORMATION_SECURITY_STANDARD.md` for threat model, control tiers and AI/research rules.
- Never commit secrets, `.env` files or service role keys to Git.
- `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY` is server-only (`apps/web/src/lib/env/server.ts` with `server-only`); never import server env or service role code in client components.
- Do not apply hosted migrations until `supabase test db` has actually passed for the same Git files. An unrun check is not a pass. MCP must not become a second schema history.
- Do not implement autonomous trading or connect production Supabase without explicit approval.

## Database

- Schema evolves only via `supabase/migrations/` (Git source of truth).
- RLS tests: `supabase/tests/database/` using synthetic authenticated users.

## Wealth and privacy

- Do not store private financial data in public browser caches; sensitive routes use `private, no-store` headers.

## G0 scope guard

- Do not add agent frameworks, paid feeds, broker links, LLM providers or live financial analytics until G0 gates in `docs/07_ROADMAP_AND_GATES.md` are satisfied.
